  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopia Country Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TradeMark Africa&apos;s Ethiopia Country Programme works to reduce trade costs and modernise supply chains for one of Africa&apos;s largest landlocked economies, aligning with the Government&apos;s Home-Grown Economic Reform Agenda and national logistics strategy. Operating primarily along the Djibouti, Berbera, and LAPSSET corridors since 2018, the Programme advances trade facilitation through a combination of physical and digital interventions, including One Stop Border Post upgrades at Moyale, Tog Wajaale, and Galafi, a climate-smart inland container depot near Jigjiga, electronic cargo tracking, an integrated border management system, and blockchain-based traceability pilots in select value chains. Complementary efforts support Ethiopia&apos;s WTO accession and AfCFTA implementation, strengthen standards and sanitary and phytosanitary capacity across key export sectors such as coffee, leather, and horticulture, and promote inclusive trade by providing safe market infrastructure and financial access for women traders and small-scale entrepreneurs at key border points.</narrative>
  </description>
